    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d654">

                <pb facs="0777" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841E.00/20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-26T17:00:00+01:00">August 26, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. For the Under Secretary. Your 101, August 24, 10 p.m.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d654-f1"/> Appreciate information. From our estimate of the
                    situation your course is what we would have suggested. Have advised Winant that
                    in view of the situation here and of our interests in Northern Ireland <pb
                        facs="0778" n="766" xml:id="pg766"/> some measure of clemency is probably
                    expedient. The British and Canadian Representatives here hold the same opinion.
                    Hanging six for one would shock public opinion.</p>
                <p>Sending airmail despatch on this subject and memorandum of conversation with de
                        Valera.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d654-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
